ratty on anonymOS: OpenGL ES over Mesa EGL, the native shell, idle-friendly redraws

1. GLES backend.  Enable wgpu's `gles` feature (ratty depends on wgpu directly
   for this; Bevy only turns on Vulkan/Metal/DX12 natively) and hand winit's
   display connection to the renderer (PlatformDisplayPlugin ->
   bevy_render::renderer::RenderDisplayHandle, from the patched bevy_render in
   anonymos-crates/, wired in with [patch.crates-io]).  With no Vulkan driver,
   wgpu then picks Mesa's EGL/GL (llvmpipe in a VM) and presents to the Wayland
   window.  The log filter drops wgpu-hal's per-frame GL texture-target
   heuristic notice (it concerns Bevy's unused shadow-map arrays).

2. Shell.  With neither --command nor [shell] program: $SHELL, unless it is the
   generic /bin/sh anonymOS seeds into every process while a native shell
   exists; then the native shell (/hos-sh = dash, else /-sh; EPIN_SHELL=native,
   as the OS's other terminals export), then /bin/zsh as a login shell
   (EPIN_SHELL=linux), then /bin/sh.  portable-pty comes from the patched copy
   in anonymos-crates/ too: its child closes inherited fds even without
   /dev/fd or close-on-exec.  The choice and the child pid are printed
   to stderr ("ratty: shell ...", "ratty: spawned shell pid=N").  The window
   also closes when the shell exits even if the PTY master never reports a
   hangup (anonymOS PTYs have no EOF/EIO on slave close): the child is polled
   with try_wait.  A failing getcwd() or an unwritable cache directory (the
   runtime asset root falls back to $TMPDIR) no longer aborts startup.

3. Font.  When the font is still the default family (DejaVu Sans Mono, which
   anonymOS does not ship) and no font files are configured, use the file named
   by $HOS_TERMINAL_FONT (the OS's terminal font, Noto Sans Mono) and its
   -Bold sibling.

4. Redraws.  New default update_mode "Auto": Continuous on a hardware GPU; on a
   software rasterizer (llvmpipe) update reactively -- at once on input, window
   events and PTY output, otherwise every software_frame_interval_ms (100) to
   pace animations -- instead of pinning the CPU at 60 fps.  The PTY reader
   thread now wakes the event loop (EventLoopProxy WakeUp) when output arrives
   or the PTY closes, so reactive modes show output immediately; "LowPower"
   therefore also makes unfocused windows reactive.
